"hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:"
3020,"**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak al-Mukharrimi, narrated to us Wahb ibn Jarir, narrated to us my father (Jarir), who said: I heard Yazid ibn Ruman narrating, on the authority of 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr (RA), who said: 'A'ishah (RA) said to me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her:

""O 'A'ishah! If it were not for the fact that your people have recently left the time of ignorance (i.e., they are new to Islam), I would have demolished the House (Ka'bah) and rebuilt it, adding to it what was taken out from it (the area of al-Hijr). Indeed, they (your people) were unable to bear its expenses. I would have made for it two doors: one to the east and one to the west, and I would have leveled it with the ground, and built it upon the foundation of Ibrahim (AS).""

Ibn al-Zubayr (RA) said: ""It was this statement that prompted me to demolish and rebuild it."" He (the narrator) said: ""So I witnessed him when he demolished it and rebuilt it. He extracted the foundation of the House like the humps of camels, layered upon one another.""

My father (Jarir) said: ""So I said to Yazid ibn Ruman, while I was circumambulating with him on that day: 'Show me what they took out from al-Hijr from it.' He said: 'I will show it to you now.' When he reached it, he said: 'This is the place.'""

My father (Jarir) said: ""So I marked it out to be approximately six cubits (in length).""

And this is how Musa ibn Isma'il narrated it: Narrated to us Jarir, narrated to us Yazid ibn Ruman, on the authority of 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr (RA).

---"
3021,"Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Musa ibn Isma'il, and it was also narrated by Yazid ibn Harun, narrated to us Jarir ibn Hazim, narrated to us Yazid ibn Rumman, from Urwah, from 'A'ishah (RA) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to her, and he mentioned the hadith, and he said: Yazid said, ""I witnessed Ibn az-Zubayr when he demolished it.""

Narrated to us az-Za'farani, narrated to us Yazid. Abu Bakr said: The narration of Yazid ibn Harun indicates that Yazid ibn Rumman heard the report from both of them together.

**CHAPTER:**"
3022,"**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl (RA), who said:
""The Ka'bah in the pre-Islamic era was built with uncemented stones, without any clay or mud mortar. It was only as large as a young camel could enter.""

He then mentioned the lengthy narration about the story of the construction of the Ka'bah. He said:
""When the army of al-Husayn ibn Numayr came, he mentioned its burning during the time of Ibn al-Zubayr (RA). Ibn al-Zubayr said: 'Indeed, 'A'ishah (RA) informed me that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: *If not for the recent conversion of your people (to Islam) from disbelief, I would have demolished the Ka'bah and rebuilt it. Verily, they left seven cubits from it in al-Hijr due to lack of funds and wood.*'

Ibn Khuthaym said: 'And Ibn Abi Mulaikah informed me, from 'A'ishah (RA), that she heard this from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).'""

He then mentioned a lengthy story."
3023,"Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari, who narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr (i.e., Ibn Bakr), who informed me Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Ubaid ibn Umayr and al-Walid ibn Ata' from al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabi'ah, who said: Abdullah ibn Ubaid ibn Umayr said: Al-Harith ibn Abdullah came as an envoy to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan during his caliphate. Thereupon Abd al-Malik said: ""I do not think that Abu Khubayb (referring to Ibn al-Zubayr) heard from Aisha (RA) what he claims to have heard from her."" Al-Harith replied: ""Yes, I indeed heard it from her."" [Abd al-Malik] asked: ""Did you hear her narrate it?"" He (al-Harith) reported that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed your people shortened the construction of the Bayt (the Sacred Kaaba), and were it not for the recency of their association with polytheism, I would have restored what they omitted of it. Then if your people after me wish to build it, come to me and I will show you what they omitted of it."" So he showed her (Aisha, RA) a portion close to seven cubits. This is the hadith of Abdullah ibn Ubaid, and he mentioned the full hadith."
